	(text "Input 3S-4S LiPo (11.1-16.8 V).  R105 100k / R106 39k on the MP2307 EN pin:\nEN_BUCK = VBAT_SW x 39/139 = x0.281.\nThis is a REGULATOR BROWNOUT / EN-lockout threshold, NOT LiPo cell protection -\nthere is no per-cell monitoring.  MP2307 (r1.9): EN LOCKOUT (buck starts/stops\nswitching) = 2.5 V typ, 2.2 / 2.7 V min/max; EN SHUTDOWN = 1.5 V typ.\nBuck stops switching when VBAT_SW falls to ~8.9 V typ, with a 7.8-9.6 V\npart-to-part spread (EN 2.2-2.7 V).  The 7.8 V worst case = 2.6 V/cell on 3S,\nwhich is below a safe cell floor - this trip only prevents buck malfunction at\nlow Vin, it does not guard the battery.  Firmware/telemetry must do LiPo cutoff.\nEN abs-max = 6 V (internal ~7 V zener):  EN_BUCK = 4.7 V @ 16.8 V, 5.6 V @ 20 V\n(both OK); 6.4 V @ 23 V abs-max VIN - add a 5.1 V zener on EN if 23 V is real."
		(at 128 85 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "e115cb12-8e48-4270-9c5d-34bd828ae69c")
	)
	(text "Buck-side OR-ing ideal diode (U803 LM74700-Q1 + Q803 AO3400A).\nPer LM74700-Q1 datasheet (SNOSD17G) Table 5-1 / Fig 5-1 / Fig 10-18:\n  ANODE (pin 6) = input, connect to FET SOURCE  -> +5V_BUCK  (Q803.S)\n  CATHODE (pin 4) = output, connect to FET DRAIN -> +5V       (Q803.D)\n  EN (pin 3) -> ANODE (always on).  GATE (pin 5) -> Q803.G.\n  C803 100nF charge-pump cap between VCAP and ANODE (datasheet 9.3.2).\n  C804 100nF ANODE-to-CATHODE bypass (recommended external capacitance).\nQ803 body diode: anode=SOURCE=+5V_BUCK, cathode=DRAIN=+5V -> forward for the\nbuck feeding the rail (startup fallback), REVERSE-biased when +5V is driven\nabove +5V_BUCK (USB via U802), so it BLOCKS the back-feed.  Datasheet 10.2:\n\"...leaving the body diode of the MOSFET to block the reverse current flow\",\ngate pulled down in <0.45 us once V(ANODE)-V(CATHODE) < ~-11 mV.\nFB (R102/R103) senses +5V_BUCK -> buck regulates its own 5.0 V.  Drop ~53 mV\n@ 1.9 A, FET-limited ~5 A.  Replaces the 1.5 A LM66100 (< worst-case +5V load).\nWhy a diode at all: MP2307 is synchronous - its HS FET body diode (SW->VIN)\nwould back-feed VIN from an externally-driven +5V when the buck is off/UVLO."
		(at 140 40 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1e157bfc-6354-43f6-bb8a-b1705d48470d")
	)
