  (text "INRUSH / SOFT-START (7.a decision):\nBUILD REQUIREMENT: the battery lead MUST use an anti-spark XT60/XT90\nconnector (pre-charge resistor in the plug).  Plug-in inrush is NOT limited\non-board: Q101's body diode (VBAT->VBAT_SW, forward) charges C101 100uF +\nC102 10uF + C103 through the diode regardless of the gate\n(I_peak ~ 170-340 A for ~5-30 us, spark ~15 mJ at 16.8 V).  A single\nreverse-polarity P-FET cannot soft-start this; the anti-spark connector does.\nC114 100nF gate-source stays: R101*C114 = 10 ms -> Q101 channel enhances over\n~7 ms = a controlled, low-EMI turn-on and a softer VBAT_SW rise into the EN\ndivider (it is NOT an inrush limiter).\nMP2307 soft-start: C115 100nF on SS (was left open).  Per datasheet r1.9\n(CSS 0.1uF -> 15 ms, ISS 6 uA, SS ramps to ~0.925 V).  t_ss ~= 15 ms: the\n+5V rail ramps 0->5 V over ~15 ms, charging C105 + C113 (~46 uF total) at\n~15 mA average instead of slamming the buck current limit (~4 A) at startup."
    (at 55 150 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "a17ab971-2455-43e7-b7c8-d25a8a1331eb")
  )
